Subject: fix(gates): resolve contract evidence from the project root, not the caller's base (WFI-059)

The verification contract's `checks[].evidence` field had two resolvers and no
specified grammar. check-contract resolved it against whatever base the caller
passed -- often the spec directory -- while prepare-panelist-input always
resolves project-root-relative. Either form therefore passed one consumer and
failed the other, with nothing rejecting the ambiguous form at authoring time.

Measured on epic-194's 2026-08-28 re-panel (bundles c1e97647/aac5658a/753117c9):
all six blind verdicts -- two vendors x three tasks -- returned NEEDS_WORK with
the same dominant Major, "required checks are recorded passes:true but the
declared evidence is absent from the bundle", against evidence that existed,
passed the Done chain, and was merely written in the grammar the other consumer
accepts. One full panel round was consumed by a path-form disagreement.

This specifies the grammar as project-root-relative and enforces it where the
fix is one line. check-contract now discovers the project root from the
contract's own location -- a contract lives at
<project-root>/specs/<feature>/verification/<task>.contract.json, so the root
is the nearest ancestor from which the contract path starts with "specs/" --
and resolves every evidence path from there. When that root differs from the
base the caller passed, each evidence failure names it:

    check 'lint' evidence file missing: verification/evidence.log
      (project-root-relative base: /path/to/project)

The note is conditional. A contract outside specs/ has no such ancestor and
falls back to the caller's base, so fixture trees are untouched; and a caller
that already passes the project root sees byte-identical messages, which keeps
the 21 golden fixtures under tests/fixtures/phase2-contract-path-golden/ green.

_pass4_risk_tier deliberately keeps the caller's root: it reads a
project-posture file, not evidence.

NOT in this patch: WFI-059 item 3, the preparer annotation naming the attempted
ABSOLUTE path. The bundle sanitizer redacts every /var, /Users, /private and
/tmp path before a bundle reaches a vendor (prepare-panelist-input.sh:1264), so
that annotation always renders "no file exists at [PATH_REDACTED]" -- strictly
less diagnosable than today's wording. Measured, not assumed. The wording needs
an owner decision; weakening the sanitizer is not on the table, because it is
what keeps host paths out of third-party vendor input.

Apply from the repository root:

    git apply --check docs/ci-staging/wfi-059-evidence-project-root.patch
    git apply docs/ci-staging/wfi-059-evidence-project-root.patch

